# {{.ProjectName}}

A drag & drop builder for Wails application UIs, generated from the Wails
`ui-builder` template.

Compose a window from desktop building blocks — toolbar, sidebar, content area,
tables, forms, status bar — tune each one in the inspector, then press **Run**
to use it against this app's Go backend: buttons call bound Go methods or emit
events, and text, badges, metrics, progress bars and consoles display the data
of Go events. **Export frontend** writes the design out as the frontend of a
Wails project.

## Getting started

```
wails3 dev      # run with hot reload
wails3 build    # produce a production binary in bin/
```

## Wiring a design to Go

| In the builder | What it does | Go side |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Button → *Call a Go method* | `Call.ByName("main.GreetService.Greet", args)`; the result is published to a channel | `application.NewService(&GreetService{})` |
| Button → *Emit an event to Go* | `data-wml-event` | `app.Event.On("name", …)` |
| Button → *Window action* | `data-wml-window="Minimise"` and friends | — |
| Button → *Open a URL* | `data-wml-openurl` | — |
| *Bind to Go event* on text, badge, metric, progress, console | Shows the payload of every event with that name | `app.Event.Emit("name", data)` |
| Toolbar → *Window drag region* | `--wails-draggable: drag` | Hidden / frameless title bars |

Arguments for a Go call are one per line; `$name` reads the control whose
*Field name* is `name`. Numbers and `true` / `false` are sent typed.

## Exporting

**Export frontend** asks for a folder and writes `<name>-frontend/` containing
`index.html`, `public/style.css`, `src/main.js`, a README with the backend
expectations, and the layout itself. Those files drop straight into the
`frontend/` directory of a project created with `wails3 init -t vanilla-js`.

## What's inside

| Path | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| `main.go` | Creates the Wails app, registers the services and emits the `time` event |
| `layoutservice.go` | `LayoutService` — save / open layouts and export frontends via native dialogs |
| `greetservice.go` | `GreetService.Greet`, the method the starter design calls |
| `frontend/src/components.ts` | The component registry: defaults, inspector fields and renderers |
| `frontend/src/theme.ts` | Stylesheet for the app UI you build (shared with the export) |
| `frontend/src/runtime.ts` | Run mode: wires buttons and bindings to the Go backend |
| `frontend/src/exporter.ts` | Generates the exported frontend files |
| `frontend/src/store.ts` | Document state, selection and undo/redo history |
| `frontend/src/canvas.ts` | Artboard rendering, selection and drag & drop |
| `frontend/src/palette.ts` · `inspector.ts` · `layers.ts` | The three panels |
| `frontend/public/style.css` | The builder's own chrome (panels, toolbar, window frame) |

Layouts are plain JSON (`*.uib.json`). The builder autosaves the current design
to the browser's local storage, so closing the app never loses work.

## Adding a component

Append an entry to the `components` array in `frontend/src/components.ts`:

```ts
{
    type: 'callout', label: 'Callout', category: 'Content', icon: 'text',
    defaults: {text: 'Heads up!', bind: ''},
    fields: [
        {key: 'text', label: 'Text', kind: 'textarea', group: 'Content'},
        {key: 'bind', label: 'Bind to Go event', kind: 'text', group: 'Wails'},
    ],
    render(node) {
        const div = document.createElement('div');
        div.className = 'ub-callout';
        div.textContent = String(node.props.text ?? '');
        if (node.props.bind) div.dataset.bind = String(node.props.bind);
        return div;
    },
},
```

Add its styles to `componentStyles` in `frontend/src/theme.ts` and it shows up
in the palette, renders on the canvas and is included in exports. Set
`container: true` (plus `direction`) for components that accept children.

## Keyboard shortcuts

Press `?` in the app for the full list. The essentials: `⌘Z` / `⇧⌘Z` undo and
redo, `⌘D` duplicate, `⌫` delete, `⌘S` save, `⌘O` open, `⌘E` export, `⌘P`
run. On Windows and Linux use `Ctrl` in place of `⌘`.

